WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.480
In 1972, a Uruguayan rugby team was on their way to Chile for a match when disaster struck.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.320
Their plane, carrying 45 passengers, crashed in the treacherous Andes Mountains.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.360
The survivors were left stranded with limited supplies and freezing temperatures.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:25.640
They knew they had to act fast to stay alive. As the days went by, they were forced to make unimaginable decisions.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.880
They knew they had to conserve their food and water, but it wasn't enough.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.740
In order to stay alive, the survivors were forced to resort to cannibalism.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.880
It was a decision that would haunt them for the rest of their lives.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:46.600
The Uruguayan rugby team was known for its camaraderie and teamwork, but in this moment they had to put aside their sportsmanship to survive.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:54.120
After 72 days, two of the survivors, Roberto Canessa and Antonio Vizintín, decided to hike for help.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:01:01.360
They trudged through the treacherous terrain for 10 days. Their journey was not easy, but they refused to give up.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:06.560
Finally, on December 23, they spotted a rescue helicopter in the distance.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.360
The two men hiked down to the helicopter and were greeted by the relief team. They had finally found help.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.880
The rescue team was amazed by the survivors' story. They knew they had to act fast

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.480
to get the rest of the survivors to safety. In total, 16 people were rescued from the Andes Mountains.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:43.000
[Closing narration and music]
